According to Article 2(2) of the GDPR, the following types of processing activities fall outside the material scope of this Regulation:

(a) Processing of personal data in the course of an activity which falls outside the scope of Union law;
(b) Processing by the Member States when carrying out activities which fall within the scope of Chapter 2 of Title V of the TEU;
(c) Processing by a natural person in the course of a purely personal or household activity;
(d) Processing by competent authorities for the purposes of the prevention, investigation, detection or prosecution of criminal offences or the execution of criminal penalties, including the safeguarding against and the prevention of threats to public security.

This information is sourced from the provided context, specifically from the section on GDPR Article 2 - Material scope.
